    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Professor El Nasir Lalani was invited as a keynote speaker at the 51st annual meeting of the Asia Pacific Advanced Network (APAN), held virtually on February 3, 2021. His presentation covered: non-communicable diseases (NCDs) and their impact on morbidity, mortality with particular reference to the low-to-middle-income countries (LMICs); potential applications of stem cells and regenerative medicine to cure NCDs; and the need for building local/regional capacity in basic sciences and translational medicine.",
